SDK FPSCR: per-arch HostToGuest rounding table (mffs on ARM64 swapped round-up/round-down).
Applied by tools/build_sdk_from_source.py (SDK_BEHAVIOUR_PATCHES). Correctness fix, no switch.

PowerPC FPSCR[RN]: 0 nearest, 1 toward zero, 2 +infinity, 3 -infinity. The host rounding
field decodes differently per arch: x86 MXCSR RC is (nearest, down, up, zero), ARM64 FPCR
RMode is (nearest, +infinity, -infinity, zero). GuestToHost was already per arch and right,
but HostToGuest lived in ppc/context.h with the x86 order, so on ARM64 mffs read +infinity
back as -infinity and vice versa, and a partial mtfsf (read-modify-write through
loadFromHost) wrote the swapped mode back. Fable II has 5 mffs and 5 mtfsf sites; the game
runs at round-to-nearest, where both tables agree, so no visible change is expected.

HostToGuest now sits next to GuestToHost in platform/fpscr.h for each arch, a static_assert
checks that the two tables invert each other for all four modes, and context.h defines
REX_FPSCR_HOST_TO_GUEST_PER_ARCH so tests can tell the fixed runtime from the prebuilt one.
Also fixes the ARM GuestToHost comment ("-Infinity, -Infinity").

